From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:49:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] riscv: Add the FonTamSOC ftpu platform

The ftpu is the RV32IMA core of the FonTamSOC, without MMU; the kernel
runs in machine mode, without firmware:
- the timebase is the frequency of the clock of the core, which its CSR
  clkfreq (0xcc0) gives, the device tree carrying no frequency; its CSR
  time counts every clock cycle, the same on every hart, and get_cycles()
  reads it in M-mode rather than a CLINT;
- its wfi waits only while mstatus.MIE is set: arch_cpu_idle() enables
  the interrupts around it, and do_irq() moves the epc of an interrupt
  taken at the wfi past it;
- its data-cache is write-back and cannot be flushed as a whole, and its
  instruction fetches read the memory: the flushes of the icache first
  write the range back, a word at a time with amoor.w, or the whole
  data-cache by reading an array of its size, then execute fence.i; with
  SMP, the data-cache of every hart is written back before any hart
  executes fence.i;
- with SMP, the secondary harts, which the bootloader parks, are woken by
  an interprocessor interrupt once their boot data is published, through
  a hook which the driver of the interrupt controller sets; and they are
  started only when /cpus states the atomic coherence of the bitstream,
  without which harts with a data-cache cannot share words between atomic
  and plain accesses, as the ticket spinlocks do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
